  "question": {
    "text": "A hypothetical gas expands adiabatically such that its volume changes from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>08</mn></math> litres to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn></math> litres. If the ratio of final pressure of the gas to initial pressure of the gas is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>81</mn></mfrac></math> . Then the ratio of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mfrac></math> will be."
  },
